---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="PixelPage vs Unbounce: A/B Testing and Speed Compared | PixelPage Blog"
  description="How does PixelPage's built-in A/B variant generator stack up against Unbounce's Smart Traffic? A quick comparison for marketers who need speed and results."
>
  <Nav />

  <article class="pt-32 pb-24 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 font-sans">
    <header class="mb-10 text-center">
      <span class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-violet-400 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-violet-500/10 border border-violet-500/20">
        A/B Testing
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mt-4 mb-4">
        PixelPage vs Unbounce: A/B Testing and Speed Compared
      </h1>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-xs text-gray-400 pb-6 border-b border-white/10">
        <span>By PixelPage Strategy Team</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>July 26, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>4 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300 space-y-6 leading-relaxed pt-2">
      <p class="text-base text-gray-200 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        Both platforms promise better conversions — but they get there completely differently.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight pt-4">Unbounce: Traffic Optimization for Existing Pages</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Unbounce</strong> built its reputation on optimization. Its Smart Traffic feature uses machine learning to route each visitor to whichever page variant is statistically likely to convert them, based on device, location, and behavior. Unbounce claims this delivers higher conversions than standard 50/50 A/B testing. It's a strong feature — but it's only available on the Experiment plan and up (~$112/month), and pages are hosted strictly on Unbounce infrastructure.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight pt-4">PixelPage: Instant Multi-Variant AI Creation</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>PixelPage</strong> approaches testing from the creation side rather than the traffic side. Its <strong>Built-In A/B Testing</strong> feature automatically generates Variant A (Control) and Variant B (Challenger) — with alternate headlines and CTA copy — the moment your page is created.
      </p>
      <p>
        You test messaging hypotheses from day one instead of setting up experiments manually. Combined with chat-based real-time AI editing, you can tweak a headline or CTA and regenerate new variants in seconds.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight pt-4">On Speed and Export</h2>
      <p>
        PixelPage's core promise is producing a production-ready page in about 10 minutes from a single prompt, with lightweight, semantic HTML/CSS export built for instant load times — no heavy page-builder overhead.
      </p>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-violet-500/10 border border-violet-500/30 text-violet-200 text-sm">
        <strong>Bottom line:</strong> Unbounce excels at optimizing traffic across existing pages long-term. PixelPage excels at getting multiple well-written, testable variants live fast — ideal for agencies and marketers who need volume without sacrificing conversion focus.
      </div>

      <div class="pt-8 border-t border-white/10 mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Want instant Variant A/B landing pages?</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">Generate A/B testable landing pages in minutes.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/chat" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-bold text-xs bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 to-fuchsia-500 text-white shadow-lg">
          Start Free Generator Studio →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
